P-009.falsifiable_test:
Run on the full val split. The hypothesis is falsified if any of the following holds:
(i) val rel_l2 ≥ 0.025;
(ii) more than 5% of samples have chi^2/n > 1.15;
(iii) more than 5% of samples have a 3-start spread > 3 GN std;
(iv) the efficiency ratio RMSE / mean CRB std falls outside [0.8, 1.3] for any parameter.

Diagnostic for the shielding counterexample: stratify the k1 error by terciles of k2 and the k4 error by terciles of k3. If one stratum has an efficiency ratio > 1.5 while its chi^2 stays near 1, that identifies flat-direction stalling rather than a local minimum.

P-010.falsifiable_test:
Run on the full val split twice with identical code and seed: estimator='mean' (this arm) and estimator='mode' (its paired control). Compute the paired bootstrap 95% CI of rel_l2(mean) - rel_l2(mode).

Falsified if any of the following holds:
(i) the CI includes 0 or the relative gain is < 2%;
(ii) the per-sample squared-error reduction is not concentrated (≥ 70% of the total) in samples whose truth lies within 2 GN std of a bound;
(iii) the gain is mostly on k2/k3 rather than k1/k4.

Sanity check: the mode arm should reproduce P-001 within ±0.002. If it does not, the solver differs and the comparison against P-004 is not apples-to-apples. Also report the distribution of the accepted-draw fraction.

P-017.falsifiable_test:
Run on the full val split. The hypothesis is falsified if any of the following holds:
(i) rel_l2 / floor_mean > 1.15;
(ii) rel_l2 >= 0.025 while rel_l2 / floor_mean > 1.05, i.e. excess error that the floor does not explain;
(iii) more than 5% of samples have chi^2/(n-4) above the chi^2_{n-4} 0.975 quantile / (n-4);
(iv) more than 5% of samples have a 3-start spread > 3 GN std;
(v) on the interior stratum, any per-parameter RMSE / mean CRB std falls outside [0.8, 1.3].

Near-bound stratum ratios are reported but are not falsifying.
